  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    grid = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find background color (most common)\n    from collections import Counter\n    bg = Counter(grid[r][c] for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols)).most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    # Find the rectangle (large block of non-bg, non-single cells)\n    # First find all non-bg cells\n    non_bg = {}\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != bg:\n                non_bg[(r,c)] = grid[r][c]\n    \n    # Find rectangle color (the one forming a large block)\n    color_counts = Counter(non_bg.values())\n    rect_color = color_counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    rect_cells = [(r,c) for (r,c),v in non_bg.items() if v == rect_color]\n    min_r = min(r for r,c in rect_cells)\n    max_r = max(r for r,c in rect_cells)\n    min_c = min(c for r,c in rect_cells)\n    max_c = max(c for r,c in rect_cells)\n    \n    # Single dots\n    dots = [(r,c,v) for (r,c),v in non_bg.items() if v != rect_color]\n    \n    for r,c,v in dots:\n        # Check if row overlaps with rectangle rows\n        if min_r <= r <= max_r:\n            # Draw horizontal line from dot to rectangle\n            if c < min_c:\n                for cc in range(c, min_c):\n                    grid[r][cc] = v\n            elif c > max_c:\n                for cc in range(max_c+1, c+1):\n                    grid[r][cc] = v\n        # Check if col overlaps with rectangle cols\n        if min_c <= c <= max_c:\n            if r < min_r:\n                for rr in range(r, min_r):\n                    grid[rr][c] = v\n            elif r > max_r:\n                for rr in range(max_r+1, r+1):\n                    grid[rr][c] = v\n    \n    return grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    import copy\n    grid = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find background color (most common)\n    from collections import Counter\n    bg = Counter(grid[r][c] for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols)).most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    # Find the rectangle (large block of non-bg, non-single cells)\n    # First find all non-bg cells\n    non_bg = {}\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != bg:\n                non_bg[(r,c)] = grid[r][c]\n    \n    # Find rectangle color (the one forming a large block)\n    color_counts = Counter(non_bg.values())\n    rect_color = color_counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    rect_cells = [(r,c) for (r,c),v in non_bg.items() if v == rect_color]\n    min_r = min(r for r,c in rect_cells)\n    max_r = max(r for r,c in rect_cells)\n    min_c = min(c for r,c in rect_cells)\n    max_c = max(c for r,c in rect_cells)\n    \n    # Single dots\n    dots = [(r,c,v) for (r,c),v in non_bg.items() if v != rect_color]\n    \n    for r,c,v in dots:\n        # Check if row overlaps with rectangle rows\n        if min_r <= r <= max_r:\n            # Draw horizontal line from dot to rectangle\n            if c < min_c:\n                for cc in range(c, min_c):\n                    grid[r][cc] = v\n            elif c > max_c:\n                for cc in range(max_c+1, c+1):\n                    grid[r][cc] = v\n        # Check if col overlaps with rectangle cols\n        if min_c <= c <= max_c:\n            if r < min_r:\n                for rr in range(r, min_r):\n                    grid[rr][c] = v\n            elif r > max_r:\n                for rr in range(max_r+1, r+1):\n                    grid[rr][c] = v\n    \n    return grid",
